{"repositoryId":554335202,"availability":"available","full":"amckenna41/iso3166-2","name":"iso3166-2","description":"A lightweight Python package, and API, for accessing all of the world's most up-to-date and accurate ISO 3166-2 subdivision data, including: name, local/other name, parent code, type, latitude/longitude, flag and history.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":34,"forks":1,"created":"2022-10-19T16:33:03Z","updated":"2026-10-13T14:52:16Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://iso3166-2-api.vercel.app/","topics":["api","countries","geographic-data","geonames","iso3166","iso3166-2","iso3166-flag-icons","iso3166-updates","json","python","regions","world-data","world-flags"],"demo":"https://iso3166-2-api.vercel.app/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T02:48:23.256Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T02:48:23.256Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T02:48:23.256Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-16T02:48:23.256Z","stars":34,"forks":1}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["iso3166-2 is a structured lightweight custom-built Python package and dataset, and accompanying RESTful API, that can be used to access all of the world's ISO 3166-2 subdivision data. A plethora of data attributes are available per country and subdivision including: name, local/other name, code, parent code, type, lat/longitude, flag and history. Currently, the package and API supports data from 250 countries/territories and >5000 subdivisions, according to the ISO 3166-1 & ISO 3166-2 standards, respectively. The software uses another custom-built Python package called iso3166-updates to…","The International Organisation for Standards defines codes for the names of countries, dependent territories, special areas of geographical interest, and their principal subdivisions [[1]](#references). The ISO 3166-2 defines codes for identifying the principal subdivisions (e.g. provinces, states, municipalities etc) of all countries coded in the ISO 3166-1. The official name of the standard is \"Codes for the representation of names of countries and their subdivisions – Part 2: Country subdivision code.\" For some countries, codes are defined for more than one level of subdivisions.","Currently, this package and accompanying API support subdivision data from 250 officially assigned code elements within the ISO 3166-1, with 200 of these countries having recognised subdivisions (50 entires have 0 subdivisions), totalling 5,046 subdivisions across the whole dataset. Transitional reservations are not included and only 4 of the exceptional reservations, that have now been officially assigned, are included: AX (Aland Islands), GG (Guernsey), IM (Isle of Man) and JE (Jersey) [[3]](#references). The ISO 3166-2 was first published in 1998 and as of November 2024 there are 5,046…"],"features":["Code - ISO 3166-2 subdivision code","Name - subdivision name","Local/other name - subdivision name in local language or any alternative name/nickname it is commonly known by","Latitude/Longitude - subdivision coordinates","Flag - subdivision flag from iso3166-flags repo; this is another ISO 3166 related custom-built dataset of over 3500 regional/subdivision flags"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/amckenna41/iso3166-2/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"db6de296a84f7b7e9503e091b9d7ef03cce0a03e6d9a0ffbaba98f305d5a90f1","extractedAt":"2026-10-16T02:48:23.336Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T02:48:23.336Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"iso3166-2 is a structured lightweight custom-built Python package and dataset, and accompanying RESTful API, that can be used to access all of the world's ISO 3166-2 subdivision data. A plethora of data attributes are available per country and subdivision including: name, local/other name, code, parent code, type, lat/longitude, flag and history. Currently, the package and API supports data from 250 countries/territories and >5000 subdivisions,